# ==========================================
# Antigravity & AI scratch directories
# ==========================================
.gemini/
scratch/

# Local working data — the whole directory, not a list of files.
#
# It holds rosters, exports, import templates and reference downloads. The
# rosters carry the actual squad's names and most of those players are minors,
# and the reference downloads are large third-party files that are stale the
# moment they land. Nothing in the codebase reads any of it: the app's data
# lives in Postgres, and the shapes these files mirror are defined by the
# import/export code in public/js/admin.js.
#
# Excluding the directory rather than naming files was a deliberate change of
# approach. Naming them meant every new spreadsheet a coach dropped here was
# untracked-and-visible until someone judged it, and a file called
# FR-SO-BHS_Player_Template turned out to hold a real roster — so the naming
# convention was not a safe filter. Default to out.
Resouces/CSV/

# Local reference material and scratch assets — source documents for the daily
# thoughts and quiz content, ad-hoc account-admin notes, and a stray image.
# The app reads none of them; the content that ships lives in Postgres.
#
# The account-admin files are working notes rather than runnable SQL, and they
# name real people by email address. That is the reason they stay out: git
# history is permanent, and a repo is a poor place to keep a coach's address.
Resouces/Thoughts4TheDay/
Resouces/SQL/resetPassword.sql
Resouces/SQL/removeUser.sql
assets/soccerPlayer.png
deployed.bat
